To pass data to the TodoList component, you can use props. Props are short for "properties" and are a way to pass data from a parent component to a child component.

In the TodoApp component, you can define a todos array and pass it as a prop to the TodoList component like this:




import React from 'react';
import TodoList from './TodoList';

const TodoApp = () => {
  const [todos, setTodos] = useState([]);

  return (
    <div>
      <TodoList todos={todos} />
    </div>
  );
};

export default TodoApp;
In the TodoList component, you can access the todos array passed as a prop like this:




import React from 'react';

const TodoList = ({ todos }) => {
  return (
    <div>
      {todos.map((todo, index) => (
        <Task key={index} todo={todo} />
      ))}
    </div>
  );
};

export default TodoList;
